    "description": "The Extension Runtime gives an untrusted Code Review Plugin access to a workspace file, a diagnostic client, and a small configuration service. The plugin receives live objects rather than copied data, and it may retain those references for the lifetime of its process. The Plugin Supervisor must be able to disable the plugin's access when the extension is unloaded or violates policy, without asking the plugin to release anything. Other extensions must continue using the same underlying workspace and services after that action, so those targets cannot be destroyed. Existing operations may finish, but every later call made through the plugin's access must fail. The control must reside with the supervisor and take effect even if the plugin ignores an unload event or continues running in a background thread.",
    "decision_statement": "Select the mechanism that lets the Extension Supervisor terminate all future access held by an untrusted plugin while preserving the underlying workspace and services for everyone else.",
    "notes": "Grantor-controlled withdrawal of live references without plugin cooperation or target destruction grounds single-reference revocation; membrane is the forced sibling for the transitive-propagation axis."
  },
